-- A comment is about a post or a photo. PostComment is a comment about a post, and its property
-- `quoted` reads the post's `body`.
--
-- The compiler refuses the read: "[F1] 'body' is declared on 'Post' separately, so it is not a
-- member of 'Content'; read it after narrowing". The refinement's own condition, `target is Post`,
-- already says every PostComment's target is a Post. A rule over PostComment, and a rule written
-- `when (Comment where target is Post)`, are refused the same read in their bodies.
act Post { body: text }

act Photo { caption: text }

shape Content = Post or Photo

act Comment { target: one Content }

shape PostComment = Comment where target is Post {
    quoted: text = target.body
}
